16 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating the connection between gut and lung compartments through microbial metabolites and the blood pathway. Healthy gut microecology supports lung health, while TB-induced dysbiosis impairs barriers, activates inflammation, exacerbates tuberculosis progression, and leads to systemic and pulmonary inflammatory responses.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Infographic detailing a multi-omics workflow for tuberculosis research, organized into four layers: core input \(genomics, metabolomics, proteomics\), intermediate integration \(pairwise correlation and three-omics regulatory network\), output application \(early diagnosis, treatment guidance, prognostic monitoring, new drug development\), and feedback regulation for clinical data to basic research improvement.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating AI and machine learning applications in tuberculosis diagnosis: A shows AI-assisted X-ray and CT imaging for early TB detection; B shows fluorescence microscopy of sputum smears for rapid bacillus quantification; C displays AI pathology analysis of lung biopsy tissue for pattern recognition; D integrates multi-modal data to support accurate differential diagnosis, improving sensitivity, specificity, and clinical decision-making.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Flowchart diagram illustrating machine learning algorithms with a central circle connecting two main modules: data input \(including genomic data, imaging data, microbiome, clinical indicators, environmental and behavioral factors\) and output decision \(personalized drug recommendations, treatment duration prediction, adverse reaction alerts, disease monitoring\). Surrounding elements include prediction models, causal inference analysis, multimodal fusion algorithms, and clinical decision support system.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 60 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating connections among technologies, gut microbiome, gut-lung communication, pulmonary tuberculosis \(TB\), and interventions. Sections detail multi-omics, AI applications, gut microbial composition, metabolite production, immune responses, intervention approaches, and shared therapeutic goals to enhance TB therapy efficacy and reduce adverse reactions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 50 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
